WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You moved for this show.
-Yeah.

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.436
-And so it's been five years.
Now you fully live in the U.K.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.406
-Yeah. I mean, I thought -- we
literally, like, put our stuff

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.407 line:92%
in storage and I told my wife,

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We'll probably be there
six months.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're gonna cancel it
immediately."

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.079
And then they didn't and now we
have been there --

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:13.813 line:92%
we've had children there.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we're totally
plugged in. Yeah.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:16.716 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And that's it.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.252
Do you miss it when you come
back for something like this?

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.954 line:92%
Do you see things that you miss?

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.090 line:92%
No, of course, I do. Absolutely.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.660
I mean, sandwiches here are
larger, which is important.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.294 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I miss the nature.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, there's wonderful nature
in the U.K.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's more rolling hills.
It's a gentler nature.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:36.202
We lived in California where you
can get eaten by an earthquake

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.037 line:92%
and killed by a tidal wave.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.806
And I, like -- nature should be
able to kill you like that.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what I'm used to.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it's
a little softer there,

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
which sometimes I have
difficulty with.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:48.615 size:81% position:41%
-You've never been to
Hampstead Heath, then.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
All happening there.
In the bushes.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You grew up in Ireland.
-Yes.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:56.122
-On a turkey farm or adjacent to
a turkey farm?

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:59.559
-No, it was -- it wasn't on top
of the turkey farm.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were plucking.
You were plucking.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:05.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you pluck?
-Yes, yeah, I plucked.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:05.732 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's how I got my money
for records and sweets.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:08.935 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Gotcha.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:12.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
And was it during the plucking
that you thought,

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.506 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"I'm gonna be a writer"?

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.641 line:92%
-It's such a natural route

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:19.112 size:75% position:38%
from poultry farming
into comedy writing.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I mean, I think
it gave me --

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:24.851
Yeah, it definitely affected
my personality that I have.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:27.654
All my brothers and sisters
and I have PTSD from that.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She'll just stare off
into the distance

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:33.026
when we're writing sometimes and
I'm like, "Is it the turkeys?"

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:33.560 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it's like,
you know, Christmas --

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you farm turkeys
for a living,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.099 line:92%
my dad -- there was five kids.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the only time
he made money.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:44.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, we have no Disneyland
in Ireland, so there was no --

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we would have been
selling legs

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
left, right and center.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:52.245 size:81% position:41%
-You just had to wait.
-Just Christmas. Yeah.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:52.912 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-And were there other --

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, obviously you guys
are both in marriages.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:55.849 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You both have kids.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
So obviously that inspired
a lot in the show.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.419
And then were there other things
that would happen

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
that would find their way
into the show?

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, did you --
Once you start going into

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
season two, three, and four
of something like this,

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:07.594
are you just -- your antenna
constantly up, hoping for things

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
to happen to you that you can
put in the show?

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:12.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean, one time I came
in to write in the morning,

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.467
and I said, "Guess what happened
to me last night.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.769
I was jogging, and a guy came up
to me on a bike

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.739
under cover of night
and squirted liquid in my face."

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:20.974 line:92%
And I was like, "Oh, my God!"

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I literally --
"It's acid!"

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:25.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "I'm probably
starting to go blind."

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:28.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"No, wait, oh, it's juice."

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:28.615 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:29.849 line:92%
And so I told Sharon that.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was, like,
"I was really scared."

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she just was laughing.
And she was like --

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.422 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.492 line:92%
-Yeah. That's episode three.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:44.097
-Do you -- I mean, obviously,
132 countries watch this show.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:47.333
So, obviously, it's a universal
topic that you're writing about,

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.236
but when you do press, like,
is it different to talk about

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.105 size:84% position:42%
the show in the U.K.
than when you come here

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:52.939 line:92%
and talk about it in the U.S.?

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:53.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do people ask you
different questions

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
about it depending
where you are?

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.445 size:81% position:41%
-Well, they -- I think
the U.S. and the U.K.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of view it
slightly differently.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:06.586
Like, an American audience seems
to get a little bit more upset

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
with us when
we're mean to each other.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:13.560
Or if we end on a bad note,
like the end of season one was.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had this horrible fight.
-Yeah.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.464
-You called me an ingrate shrew.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I called you, you know,
an American prick.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:21.801 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I can't remember.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:25.572
And then my water's broke,
and then we just ended the show.

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:26.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And, yeah.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-British people are like,
"Yes, of course.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
Naturally, yes, it's terrible.
Yes."

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:32.111
-Terrible things happen.
-Terrible things happened.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whereas American people
are like,

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:37.517
"Wait, that's -- no, we have to
go back and do it again nice."

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:38.551 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then after four seasons,
Americans are like,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, yeah, I know
what they're gonna do."

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're more used to
our misanthropic --

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like at this point
you certainly know

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:46.726 line:92%
what you're signing up for

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.094
when you're watching an episode
of "Catastrophe."

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.930
I'm assuming, as you should be,
you're very proud of the show.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are there scripts earlier
in your life?

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:54.934
Are there things you've written
that you were less proud of?

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like
that's very rewarding

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:57.403 line:92%
for young writers to hear,

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you just don't start
at this place.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:02.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, for the young writers,
yes. Many, many.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, many failed pilots,
like Rob.

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:08.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, I've got them, too.

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:10.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
One time I thought,
"You know what?

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really like
'The Wizard of Oz.'

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:13.586 size:81% position:41% line:92%
What if I rewrote it?"

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:16.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I readapted about half of
the book by L. Frank Baum

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:18.858 size:81% position:41%
and then brought it to
a production company,

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were like,
"You've got to be --

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:24.464
it's the most beloved -- they
did it better than you could.

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.999 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Go. Get out of here."

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:31.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
So my subpar adaptation of
"The Wizard of Oz"

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.773 size:78% position:39%
likely won't be seen.
-Never got produced.

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:34.440 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Believe it or not.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the first scripts
I ever wrote

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.777 line:92%
was about the Irish famine.

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:38.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:41.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, me and my writing partner
at the time thought

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:45.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
a period of mass starvation
in Ireland in 1845

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:46.619 line:92%
would be ripe for laughs.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:49.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You wrote it as a comedy?
-Wrote it as a comedy.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:53.192
-Oh, wow.
-We called it "The Good Blight."

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:53.926 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:55.061 size:81% position:41% line:92%
After "The Good Life."

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think it was, like,
a small --

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was an Irish family
on a small holding.

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a fun sort of
British landlord.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:04.470
And I'm so glad I can't remember
any of the plots

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I would, you know,
take myself out.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:10.076
-Well, sometimes those failures,
you learn lessons.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:13.112 size:78% position:39%
-You need to build --
The palace of success

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
can only be reached
with a pile of failures.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:16.149 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:19.886
Well, this success is really
one that means so much to me

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:20.687 line:92%
and to so many other people.

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:24.057
Thank you guys so much for being
here and congrats on the show.

